{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Inheritance, Polymorphism and Overloading in OOP"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear or use to talk about Inheritance, Polymorphism and Overloading in OOP."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common activities at work to a using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations.  Make the result report from the analysis of the information system, based on the customer requirements, following established rules and protocols."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Participates in simple conversations or simulated situations about the communicative topics for this level through the appropriate use of simple pronunciation aspects, and grammar and vocabulary structures. Recognizes simple ideas on requirement reports, tools for Object Oriented Programming, and other basic progamming tools."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n3le02ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Continuous and Be Going to in Affirmative."}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">  Be going to</span> and the <span class=\"strong\"> present continuous</span> are used to talk about future actions and events."}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">  \"Be going to\"</span>  to express the future when we intend or decide to do something that we did not arrange before. It is just an intention. <span class=\"strong\">Be going to</span> gives an extra emphasis on the idea of intention.<br/> This is the structure for the affirmative form:"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm going to call you."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You are only going to prepare them to use these concepts."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Today, I'm creating multiple inheritances."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject +<span class=\"strong\"> be going to + main verb in base form + </span> complement"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i>We <span class=\"strong\">are going to develop </span> a new software the next month.</i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i>I <span class=\"strong\">am going to fix </span>the network as soon as possible.</i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "On the other hand, we use the <span class=\"strong\"> present continuous </span> when we say what we planned and arranged to do at a specific time in the future. These are fixed plans with definite time and/or place. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember the structure for the affirmative form:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject + Auxiliary <span class=\"strong\"> (verb to be)</span> + main verb + <span class=\"strong\"> ing</span> + complement"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i>We'<span class=\"strong\">re talking </span> about object oriented language the next class.</i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i>They <span class=\"strong\">are designing </span> their software in the production process.</i>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Verbs with Infinitives in Negative"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "An <span class=\"strong\"> infinitive </span> is a verb that is not conjugated, it means, it never goes with the suffixes s, es, or ing. Don't forget to use the word \"to\" in front of the verb, in this case, \"to\" is not a preposition but is a part of the verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Infinitives in Negative Form </span> "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You don't have to declare the class."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You don't have to allow interfaces."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to use the negative form of the infinitive you can use the auxiliary verb of the grammar tense of your sentence (don't, doesn't, didn't), or you can add the word <span class=\"strong\">\u201cnot to\u201d</span> after the verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul> <li>You can <span class=\"strong\">choose to come </span>  to the meeting in the morning or in the afternoon. </li>  <li>You <span class=\"strong\">don't have to decide </span>  right now. </li>  <li>He <span class=\"strong\">doesn't need to come </span>  to the office today. </li>  <li>We <span class=\"strong\">didn't want to redesign </span>  the software. </li>  <li>I prefer <span class=\"strong\">not to talk </span>  about the situation. </li>  </ul>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "several"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "some; an amount that is not exact but is fewer than many"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(determiner) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As software developers team leaders, you know that for OOP there are several important concepts."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le02ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "interface"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a set of abstract methods and constants aimed to determine the functionality of a class"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You don't have to allow interfaces."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le02ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "up to you "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be someone else's responsibility to do something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(idiom) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You are only going to prepare them to use these concepts. You can choose when to do it. It's up to you."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le02ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "knowledgable"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person that knows a lot about something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Anyway, you don't need to worry about it because I'm knowledgeable about polymorphism. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le02ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "team session"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "meetings to train or lead a group about a specific topics"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Mrs. Parker is working in a brochure about inheritance with key ideas this week, so it's going to be ready for your next team session."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le02ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "inheritance"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "characteristics that descend or come from something or someone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm going to begin with Inheritance. This is the mechanism by which an object adopts some or all properties of another object."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le02ob07aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information polymorphism in OOP."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe how it works."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a small summary about it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Show your summary to your classmates and teacher."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for information."}, {"type": "text", "content": " I describe how it works."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a small summary."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I show my summary to my classmates and teacher."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n3le02ob07re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n3le02ob07re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Manager: </span> As software developers team leaders, you know that for OOP there are several important concepts. Today, I'm creating multiple inheritances; then, I'm going to call you to explain the next step so you can lead a session with your team. You don't have to declare the class, and you don't have to allow interfaces. You are only going to prepare them to use these concepts when they are designing their software in the production process."}, {"time": "32000", "image": "enpe8n3le02ob07re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "You can choose when to do it. It's up to you. You need to remember we're going to focus on Java since it is an object-oriented language that provides the features of inheritance, polymorphism, and overloading.</br>\nI know people doing this training don't have any knowledge of these features, so I'm going to explain these concepts. I'm going to begin with Inheritance. This is the mechanism by which an object adopts some or all properties of another object through hierarchical classification. With inheritance, many objects take more specialized variations from the main objects or classes. Mrs. Parker is working in a brochure about inheritance with key ideas this week, so it's going to be ready for your next team session."}, {"time": "82000", "image": "enpe8n3le02ob07re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "Finally, we need to talk about polymorphism. This feature allows a defined variable with a type of data to take the values from secondary classes that inherit the main class. Therefore, one method needs to have multiple implementations, and every class has one or several methods. Now, if you talk about overloading, it means that two methods have the same name but take different input parameters; or it can have two outcomes, and it can calculate or provide more than one version depending on the context. Anyway, you don't need to worry about it because I'm knowledgeable about polymorphism. In fact, I'm writing a handout about it this afternoon."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n3le02ob07re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about inheritance, polymorphism and overloading."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can give specific information about inheritance, polymorphism and overloading."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can recognize specific vocabulary related to inheritance, polymorphism and overloading to use it in particular situations."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What programming features are you familiar with? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "When do you think software developers use inheritance, polymorphism, and overloading for? "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "What features do we use for programming with OOP? "}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "img_path": ""}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "OOP <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">Featu